  "notes": "0.1.685b: reliable diagnostic text framing\n\nDiagnostic identity, control, and sensor replies now begin at an explicit line boundary. Native I2C error logging can no longer attach its unfinished prefix to these replies. Text frames are bounded and queued atomically; screen-capture bytes and USB update payloads retain their existing format.\n\nIncludes focused facade, protocol, and caller regression checks. A passive four-minute observation on the preceding image retained the Twin connection without Search or a radio pause. This change does not alter BLE recovery policy or conceal hardware faults.\n\nSource, exact binary hash, installed runtime observations, and publication verification are recorded separately. Full-device physical/optical QA and model-quality acceptance remain ongoing.\n",
